$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: δ-Sanshool, Compounds 20 and 21; General
Procedure A solution of the appropriate phosphonate 6, 18, or 19 (0.4
mmol) in THF (1 mL) was added to a suspension of LiOH (34 mg, 0.8 mmol)
in dry THF (5 mL) in the presence of 4 Å molecular sieves. After 20 min,
a solution of aldehyde 17 (30 mg, 0.2 mmol) in THF (1 mL) was added and
the reaction mixture was heated at reflux temperature for 3 h. After
cooling, the mixture was filtered and evaporated to dryness. The crude
residue was purified by column chromatography (CH2Cl2-MeOH, 98:2).
δ-Sanshool
(2E,4E,8E,10E,12E)-N-Isopropyltetradeca-2,4,8,10,12-pentaenamide (20)
Yield: 36 mg (70%); white solid. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 7.12-7.06
(m, 1 H), 6.09-5.96 (m, 6 H), 5.72-5.68 (m, 1 H), 5.61-5.58 (m, 2 H),
5.16 (br s, 1 H), 4.10-5.07 (m, 1 H), 2.16-2.09 (m, 4 H), 1.70 (d, J =
6.7 Hz, 3 H), 1.11 (d, J = 6.4 Hz, 6 H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ =
166.6, 141.0, 139.9, 132.4, 131.7, 131.4, 131.3, 130.1, 129.5, 129.2,
121.7, 44.7, 33.0, 23.2, 18.3. MS (ESI): m/z = 260 [M + H]+, 282 [M +
Na]+. Anal. Calcd for C17H25NO: C, 78.72; H, 9.71; N, 5.40. Found: C,
78.59; H, 9.72; N, 5.41.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, molecular sieves used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Total Synthesis of δ-Sanshool and Analogues Thereof
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Mugnaini, Claudia; Corelli, Federico
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2016), 48(13), 2085-2092

