$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the synthesis of
(E)-1-(4'-nitrostyryl)-3,5-dimethoxybenzene (8) or
(E)-1-(4'-(Methoxymethoxy) styryl)-3,5-dimethoxybenzene (14) Potassium
t-butoxide (4.28 g, 38.157 mmol) was added to a solution of (6) 5 g
(17.344 mmol) and an appropriate aldehyde (4- nitrobenzaldehyde (7) or
4-(methoxymethoxy)benzaldehyde (13) (17.344 mmol) in DMF (20 mL) at 0 °C.
The reaction mixture was warmed to room temperature and stirred for 1 h.
At the end of the reaction, the mixture was diluted with water (50 mL)
and extracted twice with EtOAc (100 mL) then, combined organic layer and
washed with brine (300 mL) and dried over Na2SO4. The crude product was
purified by flash column chromatography.
(E)-1-(4'-Nitrostyryl)-3,5-dimethoxybenzene (8) Yellow solid; Yield: 70
%. Mp 135–137 °C; 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz): δ 8.22 (2H, d, J = 9.0 Hz,
H–3', H–5'), 7.63 (d, J = 8.7 Hz, 2H, H–2', H–6'), 7.21 (1H, d, J(-
trans) = 16.2 Hz, CH=(1)), 7.11 (1H, d, J(- trans) = 16.2 Hz, CH=(2)),
6.72–6.68 (2H, m, H–2, H–6), 6.44–6.40 (1H, m, H–4), 3.85 (6H, s, 2 X
O–CH3); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75 MHz): δ 161.2 (C, C–3, C–5), 148.3 (C, C–4'),
142.8 (C, C–1'), 139.5 (C, C–1), 129.2 (CH, C–2', C–6'), 128.6 (CH=(1)),
127.2 (CH=(2)), 124.0 (CH, C–3', C–5'), 106.2 (CH, C–2, C–6), 100.0 (CH,
C–4), 56.0 (O– CH3); for C16H15NO4 MS (ESI) (m/z) 286 [M + H]+.
